## Why This Is Asked

Tests lock-free IPC design, precise memory ordering, and verification under contention.

## Key Concepts

- lock-free primitives, per-slot sequencing, memory barriers, mmap-based IPC, cache coherence.
- detection of partial writes and ensuring visibility under contention.

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct { uint64_t seq; char payload[256]; } slot_t;

void write_slot(slot_t *s, void *data, size_t n){
  __atomic_store_n(&s->seq, 0, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
  memcpy(s->payload, data, n);
  __atomic_store_n(&s->seq, 1, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
}

bool read_slot(slot_t *s, void *out){
  uint64_t a = __atomic_load_n(&s->seq, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE);
  if (a != 1) return false;
  memcpy(out, s->payload, 256);
  uint64_t b = __atomic_load_n(&s->seq, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE);
  return (a == b && a == 1);
}
```

